    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "The player fetched Taiga (which produces R/G) when they need blue mana for Echo of Eons (which costs {4}{U}{U} or flashback {2}{U}). The reasoning even says 'I need that Island for Echo of Eons' but then fetches a non-Island land. Underground Sea produces U/B and is an Island, which would provide the blue mana needed for Echo of Eons. With Lion's Eye Diamond in hand, the plan is likely to flash back Echo of Eons using LED for blue mana, but having Underground Sea as a backup blue source would be strictly better than Taiga here since there's no green cards in hand and the key card requires blue.",
      "action_taken": "Fetched Taiga (Mountain/Forest, produces R/G) off Scalding Tarn",
      "better_line": "Fetch Underground Sea (Island/Swamp, produces U/B) to have access to blue mana for Echo of Eons. The LED can provide blue mana too, but Underground Sea gives more flexibility and is the correct fetch when your game plan revolves around casting a blue spell.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 6,
      "player": "MiniMx Sarge",
      "decision_index": 8,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Wooded Foothills instead of Urza's Saga as the turn 1 land drop delays the Saga's progression by a full turn. Urza's Saga is strongest when played early to start its lore counter clock - chapter I provides colorless mana immediately, chapter II creates constructs on turn 2, and chapter III tutors for a 0/1-cost artifact on turn 3. With 4 other lands in hand, there's no shortage of land drops for future turns.",
      "action_taken": "Played Wooded Foothills as the turn 1 land drop",
      "better_line": "Play Urza's Saga as the turn 1 land drop to start the saga clock immediately, then cast both Lotus Petals. Save fetchlands for later turns when they can also thin the deck after seeing more cards.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 14,
      "player": "GPT41m Analyst",
      "decision_index": 11,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Brainstorm before playing a land is a sequencing mistake. MiniMx Sarge has two lands in hand (Bloodstained Mire and Commercial District) and could play one first. More importantly, playing a fetchland (Bloodstained Mire) first would allow them to shuffle away unwanted cards put back on top with Brainstorm. By casting Brainstorm first, they lose the ability to use the land drop this turn as a shuffle effect — they'd have to crack the fetchland they put down after Brainstorm without the option to fetch-shuffle away the cards they put back. The optimal line is: play Bloodstained Mire first, then cast Brainstorm (using Taiga for U via Mox Opal or Taiga for G... wait, Taiga produces R or G, and Mox Opal needs metalcraft which requires 3 artifacts — they have Mox Opal and Lion's Eye Diamond, only 2 artifacts, so metalcraft is not active). Actually, Taiga produces R or G, not U. To cast Brainstorm they need U. With no metalcraft on Mox Opal (only 2 artifacts), they can't produce U at all right now. Wait — let me reconsider. They have Taiga (R/G), Mox Opal (needs 3 artifacts, they have 2), and Lion's Eye Diamond (discard hand for 3 mana). To cast Brainstorm for U, they'd need to crack LED discarding their hand, which would mean they discard everything including Brainstorm. So they can't actually cast Brainstorm right now without some trick. Unless there's something I'm missing about the mana. Actually, looking again at the decision — the game is offering Brainstorm as a valid cast option, so presumably they can pay U somehow. Perhaps Taiga can be used through some other means, or maybe I'm wrong about Taiga. Taiga is Mountain Forest, producing R or G. They genuinely cannot produce U with this board unless LED is used. If LED is used, they discard hand first. This seems like perhaps a game engine issue, or I'm missing something. Given the game engine offered it as valid, let me assume they can cast it. In that case, sequencing land before Brainstorm is still better to enable a shuffle.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Brainstorm before playing a land",
      "better_line": "Play Bloodstained Mire first, then cast Brainstorm, then crack Bloodstained Mire to shuffle away unwanted cards put on top",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 24,
      "player": "MiniMx Sarge",
      "decision_index": 16,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "MiniMx Sarge had the LED + Echo of Eons flashback combo available this turn. By keeping LED in hand and Echo in hand, they could play LED (achieving Metalcraft with 3 artifacts), then crack both LEDs for mana (discarding Echo to graveyard), and flashback Echo of Eons for {2}{U} using the 6 mana from LEDs. Instead, they put Echo on top of their library, missing the combo this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Put Echo of Eons back on top of library during Brainstorm resolution, keeping Burning Wish/Commercial District/LED instead.",
      "better_line": "Put back Commercial District and Burning Wish, keep Echo of Eons and Lion's Eye Diamond. Then play LED from hand, crack both LEDs (discarding Echo to graveyard), and flashback Echo of Eons for {2}{U} to draw 7 fresh cards this turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
