    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "MiniMx Sarge has a winning combo line available this turn: Cast Lion's Eye Diamond (free), then cast Burning Wish for {1}{R} (using Taiga + Underground Sea or other mana), and while Burning Wish is on the stack, crack both Lion's Eye Diamonds discarding hand to generate {U}{U}{U} (or {U}{U}{U} from one and more from the other). This lets them flash back Echo of Eons from graveyard for {2}{U} after it's discarded, drawing 7 fresh cards and likely winning. By playing Commercial District (which enters tapped and sacrifices City of Traitors... wait, there's no City of Traitors here), the land enters tapped so it doesn't help with mana this turn. More critically, playing the land first means when they later try to execute the combo, they'll have one fewer card in hand (Commercial District is on the field instead of hand), but the real issue is that Commercial District enters tapped and provides no immediate mana benefit. The correct line is: Cast Lion's Eye Diamond (now control LED, LED, Mox Opal = 3 artifacts, enabling Metalcraft on Mox Opal). Then cast Burning Wish using Taiga ({R}) + Underground Sea ({U} or {B}) for {1}{R}. Hold priority, crack both LEDs for {U}{U}{U} + {U}{U}{U} (or appropriate colors), discarding hand (Echo of Eons goes to graveyard). Burning Wish resolves to get a sorcery (or use the mana for Echo flashback). Actually, Burning Wish gets a sorcery from outside the game - but Echo of Eons is in hand and would be discarded to LED. Then flash back Echo of Eons from graveyard for {2}{U} using the LED mana. This draws 7 fresh cards with tons of mana floating. Playing the tapped land first doesn't enable this line any better and wastes the land drop before seeing what the combo yields.",
      "action_taken": "Played Commercial District (enters tapped) as the first action of the turn.",
